# xp_gauge_streamer

C++17 X-Plane 12 plugin for **macOS (arm64 only), Windows x64 and Linux x64**. Shown in-sim as
**Welly's Gauge Streamer**. Captures the Laminar GNS430/530 and airliner CDU,
streams MJPEG to a browser frontend, and forwards presses back over WebSocket.

Same guidance as [CLAUDE.md](../../CLAUDE.md) for Claude Code.

## Commands

```bash
make setup     # SDK, civetweb, Catch2, json, ImGui, libjpeg-turbo
make build     # → build/xp_gauge_streamer.xpl
make test      # Catch2 unit tests (no SDK link)
make install   # Code-sign + deploy plugin, web/, default settings
make format    # clang-format over src/
make lint      # clang-tidy (bugprone-* and performance-* are errors)
make sanitize  # unit tests under ASan + UBSan
make release VERSION=x.y.z
```

Validate the plugin in X-Plane 12. Unit tests cover domain logic only.

## Architecture

Namespace `xp_gauge_streamer`. Network threads must never call XPLM.

- **`main.cpp`** — Entry points; `follow_viewers` enables readback / MCDU reading only while viewers are open
- **`avionics_capture`** — Draw callbacks for framebuffer devices; raw RGB on main thread; `set_readback_enabled`
- **`toliss_mcdu_source`** — Reads ToLiss `AirbusFBW/MCDU<n>` screen datarefs on main thread; `toliss_mcdu_screen` (SDK-free) builds the 24×14 grid
- **`device_presence`** — Which devices the loaded aircraft has; thread-safe
- **`frame_pipeline`** — Per-device encoder threads (libjpeg-turbo); `publish_frame` / `latest_jpeg`
- **`http_server`** — civetweb: static `web/`, `/stream/<slug>` (MJPEG), `/screen/<slug>` (SSE text), `/devices`, `/control` (no auth)
- **`command_dispatch`** — Queue presses from network → resolve lazily + execute on main thread; whitelist via `command_catalog`
- **`device_registry`** — device table (`slug`, `type`, `command_prefix`, `ScreenSource`); SDK-free `DeviceId`
- **`plugin_ui`** — Dear ImGui settings window
- **`settings`** — `<X-Plane>/Output/xp_gauge_streamer/settings.cfg`

**Frontend:** plain `web/` (no framework). Bezels in `web/bezels/<type>.json`. Text devices render via `text_screen.js` (SSE on `/screen/<slug>`).

**Threading:** capture + XPLM on main thread; encode + HTTP off-thread; presses only via `press_button`.

## Build Details

- CMake 3.21+, C++17. macOS 12.0+ **arm64 only** (no Universal Binary — Intel Macs
  cannot load it), Windows 10+ x64 (MSVC 2022), Linux x64 (GCC 11+)
- `sdk/` and `vendor/` from `make setup`, not committed
- libjpeg-turbo built from vendored source via ExternalProject, linked statically;
  its own CMakeLists refuses `add_subdirectory`. SIMD needs NASM on x64.
- Only macOS is used in anger; Windows verified in a cloud VM, Linux best effort
- `.xpl` not ASan-instrumented — use Instruments.app for in-sim analysis

## Code Quality

- **Single responsibility**: each function does one thing; each module owns one concern.
- **Meaningful names**: plain English — no abbreviations, no cryptic suffixes.
- **Small functions, shallow nesting**: early returns and helpers over deep conditionals.
- **DRY**: extract shared logic; don't abstract speculatively.
- **Encapsulation**: statics private to the translation unit; expose only what the header promises.
- **Separation of concerns**: UI never does file I/O; data modules never draw.
- **Minimal comments**: comment only non-obvious *why*.
- **No speculative generality**: match existing style; no hypothetical abstractions.
- **Boundaries only for validation**: trust internals; validate at edges.
- **Platform differences in their own translation units or one leaf seam — never in
  domain code.** `opengl.hpp` includes the GL header, `gl_entry_points` resolves the
  GL 1.5 functions, `network_info` is two files behind one header. A new `#ifdef` in
  a module doing real work is a defect.
